    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for July 21, 2026, is anchored by **Gleyber Torres** (67.52) and **Bryce Harper** (66.83), both of whom offer the highest efficiency scores of the day. **Gleyber Torres** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against D. Peterson, leveraging a +12% SP skill boost and a +13% platoon advantage to solidify his spot at the top of the order. **Bryce Harper** continues to provide high-floor production, with his xWOBA (0.386) and favorable park factors keeping him in the elite tier despite a respectable matchup against Wrobleski. **Jonathan Aranda** (61.34) remains a key value play as he hits second, benefiting from a high-order bonus and a favorable platoon look against Gausman, justifying his start in the UTIL slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Lawrence Butler**, whose score of 38.09 fell just shy of the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor.\" While **Lawrence Butler** shows potential, he was squeezed out by a combination of a tough matchup against the lefty Drake and a bottom-third-of-the-order placement that suppressed his run-scoring ceiling. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the injury status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, whose absence leaves a void in the middle of our production. As we prioritize stolen bases to combat league scarcity, keep an eye on **Masyn Winn** and **Kyle Karros**; both carry lower baseline projections but are boosted by high-efficiency indicators for base-stealing opportunities (85% and 100% respectively) against pitchers with slow deliveries.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, as several players face elite arms or neutral park environments. **Cal Raleigh** (48.74) and **JJ Bleday** (44.54) are skating near the bottom of our startable range. **Cal Raleigh** must contend with a difficult matchup against Burns, and **JJ Bleday** is dealing with a significant -14% dynamic platoon drag. **Daulton Varsho** (51.97) and **Gavin Sheets** (54.42) are serviceable, but their performance hinges on neutralizing the SP skill of Rasmussen and L\u00f3pez, respectively. We are operating with a full lineup, but with **Tyler Freeman** and others sidelined, the depth of the roster will be tested if any of these marginal starts underperform early in the slate.",
